# Two-page data sheet of an indoor air quality sensor. The key features are a side box (Side: right) that the
# overview runs beside, and the next heading goes below it (Below side boxes); its list marks each feature with a
# check drawn in SVG (Marker: image). The front view and the dimension drawing are one Figure with a Block (two SVG
# images side by side). The specification tables group their rows with cells that span several rows or columns
# (Span: 3 1, Span: 1 2), share their borders (Merge borders, from a rule) and align each column (Column align, and
# For column for the signals in IBM Plex Mono); the ordering table carries the EAN-13 barcode of each variant in a
# cell, with its digits under the bars (Readable text). The header with the logo and the document number and the
# footer with the revision and "Page 1 of 2" are Page overlay of the document.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 30mm 16mm 20mm 16mm
	Title: AQ-210 Indoor Air Quality Sensor · Data sheet
	Subject: Specifications, wiring and ordering information of the AQ-210 CO₂, temperature and humidity sensor
	Author: Kestrel Sensing Ltd
	Keywords: CO2 sensor, NDIR, Modbus RTU, BACnet MS/TP, data sheet
	Language: en
	Page overlay:
		Id: header
		Offset: -21mm 0 auto 0
		Style: header
		Stack:
			Vertical: center
			Gap: 8
			Item:
				Image: documents/datasheet/kestrel.svg
					Alt: Kestrel Sensing
					Style: logo
			Item:
				Grow: 1
				Text: Kestrel Sensing
					Style: company
			Item:
				Text: Data sheet DS-AQ210-EN
					Style: doc-number
	Page overlay:
		Id: footer
		Offset: auto 0 -12mm 0
		Style: footer
		Stack:
			Horizontal: justify
			Item:
				Text: Revision C · 2026-09-15 · Specifications may change without notice · kestrel-sensing.example
			Item:
				Text: Page {page} of {pages}
	Section:
		Block:
			Id: hero
			Style: hero
			Text: Building automation · Air quality
				Style: eyebrow
			Heading 1:
				Text: AQ-210 Indoor Air Quality Sensor
			Text: CO₂, temperature and relative humidity in one wall-mounted unit, with Modbus RTU and BACnet MS/TP on the same terminals.
				Style: tagline
		Heading 2:
			Text: Overview
		Block:
			Id: features
			Style: features
			Side: right
			Text: Key features
				Style: box-label
			List:
				Style: checks
				List item:
					Text: Dual-beam NDIR CO₂ sensor, no recalibration for 15 years
				List item:
					Text: ±(30 ppm + 3%) CO₂ accuracy
				List item:
					Text: Modbus RTU and BACnet MS/TP, chosen by DIP switch
				List item:
					Text: Two 0–10 V outputs and one relay
				List item:
					Text: Three-colour status ring
				List item:
					Text: 24 V AC/DC, under 1.2 W
		Paragraph: The AQ-210 measures carbon dioxide, temperature and relative humidity in offices, classrooms and meeting rooms, and sends them to the building management system so that ventilation follows the people in the room rather than a timetable.
		Paragraph: Its dual-beam NDIR cell compares the measuring beam with a reference beam on every reading, so it does not drift with age and needs no automatic baseline correction. This makes it suitable for rooms that are never empty, such as hospital wards and control rooms.
		Paragraph: The coloured ring on the front tells the people in the room how fresh the air is: green below 800 ppm, amber up to 1,200 ppm and red above. The thresholds can be changed over the bus, and the ring can be turned off.
		Heading 2:
			Text: Dimensions
			Below side boxes: true
		Figure:
			Id: fig-views
			Alt: Front view of the AQ-210 showing the CO₂ reading on its display, and a dimension drawing of the front and the side: 86 by 86 mm, 27 mm deep
			Caption: Front of the unit and its dimensions in millimetres. It fits a standard single back box.
